From: Douglas Teles <dga.teles@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: rk817: settle the codec around the external amplifier

The RK3562 consoles popped when the speaker path came up or went down:
the external amplifier was switched together with the codec and heard
its output settle. Switch it on 100 ms after the path is up, as the vendor codec waits
(hp-mute-delay-ms), and off 20 ms before it goes down.

---
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/rk817_codec.c	2026-11-24 12:32:20.619727241 -0300
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/rk817_codec.c	2026-11-24 12:32:20.633656960 -0300
@@ -133,8 +133,19 @@
 	if (!rk817->spk_ctl_gpio)
 		return 0;
 
-	gpiod_set_value_cansleep(rk817->spk_ctl_gpio,
-				 SND_SOC_DAPM_EVENT_ON(event) ? 1 : 0);
+	/*
+	 * The amplifier hears the codec's output settle: switch it on 100 ms
+	 * after the path is up (the vendor codec's hp-mute-delay-ms), and off
+	 * a little before the codec goes down. Without the pauses the
+	 * speaker pops.
+	 */
+	if (SND_SOC_DAPM_EVENT_ON(event)) {
+		msleep(100);
+		gpiod_set_value_cansleep(rk817->spk_ctl_gpio, 1);
+	} else {
+		gpiod_set_value_cansleep(rk817->spk_ctl_gpio, 0);
+		msleep(20);
+	}
 	return 0;
 }
 
